  {
    "pid": "arabia_v1_00",
    "label": "Arabia SAM",
    "created": "2015/01/01",
    "updated": "2026/02/05",
    "author": "TMiller",
    "modified_by": "STEP Inc, ageekhere",
    "description": "NOTE:\nRRT_Events_Arabia.xml was wrong and was removed, however the map is still unstable\n\nDuring the 1930's the Ghawar oil field, largest in the world, was discovered in eastern Saudi Arabia. Oil wells were developed by ARAMCO (the Arabian American Oil Company) and oil exporting began. Oil is still being pumped from the Ghawar field and accounts for most of Saudi Arabian exports. Kuwait, Qatar, United Arab Emirates, Iraq and Iran also export oil and are included in this map. Build a railroad to help develop the region. In addition to oil you will need to move dates, livestock, milk, and grain grown in the \"Wadis\", the Oases of the desert. Wadis are valleys where scarce water may be found after rare rainfalls or pumped from wells. Late in the game you will need to move pilgrims to Mecca and Medina, and build some of the rail projects currently planned by the Saudi Arabian Railway Organization.",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/arabia_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/arabia_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 16
  },
  {
    "pid": "arizona_gold_v1",
    "label": "Arizona_Gold_v1.7z",
    "description": "Arizona Gold Scenario:\n\n1871 – The Civil War has taught the nation that if it wishes to hold the Pacific Coast firmly to the Union, efficient transport will have to be provided, to limit the chance that some foreign country might annex California. Due to concerns of the Indian Reserves, construction is slow up to 1881, but then the Atlantic Pacific Railroad is rushed to completion with princely subsidies of land and money.\n\n1930 – To counter the Great Depression, the U.S. Government finances Hoover Dam Project. Las Vegas receives thousands of depression-weary job seekers, who help build the world’s largest gravity dam.\n\n1970 – Tourism comes of age as major economic activity, in Las Vegas and in beautiful Arizona.",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/arizona_gold_v1/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/arizona_gold_v1",
    "lunr_id": 17
  },
