  {
    "pid": "cadiz_v1_00",
    "label": "CADIZ SAM",
    "created": "2015/01/04",
    "updated": "2015/01/04",
    "author": "Diego J.",
    "modified_by": "STEP Inc",
    "description": "This map has been made with an image DEM of province of Cadiz and some Malaga, in southern Spain. It's my first map. Hope you like. \nThis map has two parts:\n\nIn the first part, we connect four cities, deliver carloads of food and buy two industries producing food, a grain processing and meat processing.\nIn the second we acquire a steel mill and a car factory, send 200 wagons of cars to any destination, make Ronda a Metropolis and connecting all cities.\n\nGood Luck.\n\nSid Meiers Railroads\nSCENERY/MAP: CADIZ\nCREATED BY: Cabo (Diego J.)\n\n*********************\n*README FILE ENGLISH*\n*********************\n\nOBJECTIVE OF THE SCENARIO.\nThis scenario consists of two phases. 1st Phase: 1850-1880 and 2nd phase: 1881-1945\n\n* First phase 1850-1880.\n\n\t- Construct two food producing industries, a grain processing and other meat.\n\t- Transport 30 loads of food.\n\t- Connect these four cities: Algeciras, Estepona, Barbate and port.\n\n* Second phase 1881-1945.\n\n\t- Build a steel mill and an auto plant.\n\t- Trasnport carloads 150 of automobiles.\n\t- Make a metropolis Round.\n\t- Connect all cities.\n\nVERSIONS\n\nCADIZ V.1.01\n------------\n\n- Removed 4 locomotives.\n- Lowered target vehicles carrying 150 (previously 200).\n- The villages accept and produce passenger.\n\nCADIZ V.1\n---------\n- Removed some locomotives.\n- Changed connection target cities in the second phase, now we have to connect all cities.\n- Changed target vehicles carrying 200 (previously 250).\n\nCADIZ v.3 (BETA)\n---------\n- We have created a safe event file \"RRT_Events_CADIZ.xml\"\n- Reference is made to file certain events (\"RRT_Events_CADIZ\") in the \"RTT_Scenario_User_CADIZ.xml\"\n- Fixed the file \"RRT_Names_CADIZ.xml\" containing in addition to the cities mentioned in \"RRT_Cities_CADIZ.xml\" other inputs, the latter being eliminated.\n- New industries have been created so that all industry is available on the stage from the beginning.\n\n- Transportation of 250 vehicles cualqier city.\n- Connect: Ronda, Benaojan, Castellar and Algeciras\n\nCADIZ v.2 (BETA)\n---------\n- Translated into English\nPresents the errors described in CADIZ v.3\n\nCADIZ (BETA)\n-----\n- First version. In Spanish.\n\n*/*\n19.08.2012",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/cadiz_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/cadiz_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 32
  },
  {
    "pid": "cajun_country_v1_00",
    "label": "Cajun Country SAM",
    "created": "2018/06/14",
    "updated": "2018/06/14",
    "author": "Slider38",
    "modified_by": "Slider38",
    "description": "Develop the Louisiana Bayous. This map contains 3 Eras with new goods, industries, engines and train cars. It runs from 1929 to 2005. This is designed as a single player stand alone map.\n\nCajun Country Goods List\n\nPassengers         from towns, cities & metros    to towns, cities & metros\nMail               from towns, cities & metros    to towns, cities & metros\nVisitors           from towns, cities & metros    to towns, cities & metros\nWood               from logging camp\t          to Lumbermill\nLumber             from lumbermill                to villages, towns, cities & metros\nLumber             from lumbermill                to lumber port\nGrain              from lumber port               to food plant\nFood               from food plant                to villages, towns, cities & metros\nWood               from logging camp\t          to wood pulp plant\nWood Pulp          from wood pulp plant           to papermill\nPaper              from papermill\t\t  to newspaper\nCattle             from cattleranch               to stockyard\nFood               from stockyard                 to villages, towns, cities & metros\nCotton             from cotton plantation         to textile mill\nTextiles           from textile mill              to port\nSteel              from port                      to steel pipe plant\nSteel Pipe         from steel pipe plant          to towns, cities & metros\nOil                from oil well                  to oil refinery\nPetrochemicals     from oil refinery              to chemical plant\nChemcials          from chemical plant            to plastic packaging plant\nPlastic Packaging  from plastic packaging plant   to cities & metros\nChemicals          from chemical plant            to paint factory\nPaint              from paint factory             to towns, cities & metros\nSteel              from port                      to machinery plant\nMachinery          from machinery plant           to port\nAuto Parts         from port                      to auto factory\nAutomobiles        from auto factory              to cities & metros\nCotton             from cotton plantation         to port\nManufactured Goods from port                      to towns, cities & metros\nGravel             from gravel dredge             to villages, towns, cities & metros\nShrimp             from shrimp boat               to towns, cities & metros\nSoldiers           from Fort Polk                 to towns, cities & metros\n\nGoods Chains\n\t\nWood     makes    Lumber    makes     Grain    makes     Food\nWood     makes    Wood Pulp   makes   Paper\nCattle   makes    Food\nCotton   makes    Textiles   makes  Steel   makes   Steel Pipe       \nOil      makes    Petrochemicals    makes    Chemicals   makes   Plastic Packaging  \nOil      makes    Petrochemicals    makes    Chemicals   makes   Paint\nCotton   makes    Textiles   makes  Steel    makes    Machinery   makes   Auto Parts   makes   Automobiles\nCotton   makes    Manufactured Goods\n\nAt the Port                             At the Lumber Port\n\nExports\t\tImports                 Export       Import\nTextiles\tSteel                   Lumber       Grain\nMachinery\tAuto Parts\nCotton\t        Manufactured Goods",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/cajun_country_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/cajun_country_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 33
