    "description": "Develop the economy of California, from the Gold Rush to the growth of tourism in the 1880s.\n\nNOTES\n- This scenario uses 'slow time', so that each month takes three times as long as normal.  Engine maintenance costs are adjusted accordingly.\n- The smelter produces one load of gold per four loads of ore delivered.  All other industries produce just one load of output for every two loads of input.\n- Delivering passengers to a gold mine increase gold production (one additional load of ore per each load of passengers).",
