  {
    "pid": "rift_valley_revisited_2_v1_00",
    "label": "Rift Valley Revisited SAM2",
    "created": "2010/09/17",
    "updated": "2010/09/17",
    "author": "Bushdoctor/Jancsika",
    "modified_by": "STEP Inc",
    "description": "Build a Railroad Empire in Rift Valley.\t\nThis scenario was designed to be played at Mogul/Hard/No AI.\n\t\n- Careful: Money is tight and things are expensive.\n- Manage your lines well and think ahead.\n- Some of your trains will never be profitable. Deal with that.\n- Regular passengers are slow workers.\n- Specialists are fast workers but are harder to find.\n- Hardbottle makes for a tricky start. Instructions at bottom.\n- Original scenario by Jancsika - Revisited version by Bushdoctor.\n- Have fun!\n\nCompleting the first era when starting at Hardbottle.\n------------- Careful: Spoiler Alert.---------------\n\nFollow the canyon, pass through Hobbiton and connect with Harland.\nBuild depots in Hobbiton and Harland. Now sell all of your track\nnorth of your depot in Hobbiton, including your original Terminal.\nThis will generate the cash to upgrade both remaining depots to \nstations. Run a passenger train between the two and use its income \nto connect Harland to Farland. Finally, build a station in Farland.\nFirst era complete.\n\nGood luck!",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/rift_valley_revisited_2_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/rift_valley_revisited_2_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 154
  },
  {
