  {
    "pid": "the_gold_king_v1_00",
    "label": "The Gold King SAM",
    "created": "2014/08/07",
    "updated": "2014/08/07",
    "author": "Slider38",
    "modified_by": "Slider38",
    "description": "In the mid 1870s, Jacob Waltz walked out of the Superstition Mountains carrying a sack of gold.  This was repeated many times over the next 10 years.  When Waltz died in 1891 the legend of the Dutchman's Lost Gold Mine began.  In 1892 the Black Queen gold mine was established in the Superstitions and the gold rush was on.  Prospectors flocked to the area staking claims in the mountains.  The railroads vied to supply the gold camps with needed goods and to haul the gold ore coming out of the mountains.  Outwit your opponents and prosper hauling the needed goods.  Take control of the map and you will be the Gold King.\n\nThe Gold King - Goods/Industries List\t\t\t\n\nIndustry\tProduces\tDeliver to\t\n\tGood\t\t\n\nSawmill\tTimbers\tGold Mine\t\n\n     'Gold Mine\tGold Ore\tGold Smelter\t\n\n     'Gold Smelter \tGold\tBank\t\n\nSawmill\tTimbers\tSilver Mine\t\n\t\t\t\n     'Silver Mine\tSilver Ore\tSilver Smelter\t\n\t\t\t\n     'Silver Smelter\tSilver\tBank\t\n\nCattleranch\tLivestock\tSlaughterhouse\n\n     'Slaughterhouse\tFood\tTown, city, metro\n\nSheepfarm\tWool\tIndian Camps\n\n     'Indian Camps\tIndian Blankets\tGeneral Store\n\n     'General Store\tTools\tMiners Camps\n\nVillages and Towns\tMiners\tMiners Camps\n\nVillages, Towns\tMail\tVillages, Towns\nCities & Metros\tPassengers\tCities & Metros\n\nDistillery\tWhiskey\tSaloons\n\nLivery Stables\tHorses\tForts\n\n     'Forts\tSoldiers\tTowns & Cities",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/the_gold_king_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/the_gold_king_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 183
  },
  {
    "pid": "the_great_northern_v1_00",
    "label": "The Great Northern SAM",
    "created": "2022/02/24",
    "updated": "2022/02/24",
    "author": "slider38",
    "modified_by": "slider38",
    "description": "The Great Northern is designed as a one player SAM which runs in 3 Eras from 1900 to 1970.  This map does not allow crossovers.  To cross existing track you must switch through.\n\t\n\tThe map is 17 x 17 and provides for some long runs.  You will likely need to build some industries in order to meet your goals.  It contains some new industries, engines, etc.\n\t\n\tThe Great Northern was the only transcontinental railroad built without any direct payments from the government.  To add a financial component to the game, you are required to have a certain amount of stock ownership. \n\t\n\tThere is a companion map entitled Great Northern AI which is designed for play against AI opponents.  I hope you enjoy The Great Northern.\n\nThe Great Northern Dual Map\n\nWood       \t\tmakes Lumber\tmakes Wood Products\nWood\t\tmakes Paper\tmakes Newspapers\nWood \t\tmakes Paper\tmakes Paper Packaging\nIron Ore\t\tmakes Steel\tmakes Automobiles\nIron Ore\t\tmakes Steel\tmakes Buses\nIron Ore\t\tmakes Steel\tmakes Steel Tanks\nIron Ore\t\tmakes Steel\tmakes Tractors\t\tmakes Farm Equipment\nIron Ore\t\tmakes Oil\t\tmakes Chemicals\t\tmakes Vinyl\t\tmakes Vinyl Windows\nCorn\t\tmakes Manuf Goods\nWheat\t\tmakes Flour\tmakes Food\nCattle\t\tmakes Food\nHogs \t\tmakes Spam\nGypsum \t\tmakes Drywall\n\n\nPlease note that the Goods Oil, Chemicals, Vinyl and Vinyl Windows are not use in The Great Northern AI version of the map.",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/the_great_northern_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/the_great_northern_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 184
  },
  {
    "pid": "the_great_northwest_v1_00",
    "label": "The Great Northwest",
    "created": "2024/04/04",
    "updated": "2024/04/04",
    "author": "slider38",
    "modified_by": "slider38",
    "description": "Railroads arrive in the Great Northwest.  This map runs in 3 Eras from 1890 thru 1950.  This map is a SAM and was\n\tdesigned as a single-player map.  There are no crossovers.  To cross existing track you must switch through.  Tunnels are expensive.  Use them \n\tsparingly.  You will probably want to build some industries.  I found through testing that it was sometimes advantageous to remove old trains\n\tand possibly unneeded track.  Be aware that the good \"Brick\" can only be delivered to Metros and Cities.  At the start of the map neither \n\texists.  I hope you enjoy The Great Northwest.",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/the_great_northwest_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
