    "pid": "wnyp_revision_2_v1_00",
    "label": "Western New York and Pennsylvania Railroad",
    "created": "2011/12/27",
    "updated": "2011/12/27",
    "author": "NSrailfan",
    "modified_by": "NSrailfan",
    "description": "This is a map of the Western New York And Pennsylvania Railroad ( WNYP ). \nThe Western New York and Pennsylvania railroad began operations in \n2001, and is still operating today and is a small shortline / Class III \nrailroad with 330 miles of track. It's headquarters is in Falconer, New York.\n It is not an independent railway though, it is controlled by the  Livonia, \nAvon and Lakeville Railroad. \n\nThe main challenge of this map is to run it like you would in real life. \nTry to have only one of engine on the map at a time and try to make it \nmainly single line, with some double track.\n\nI would like to thank Snoopy55 for painting the engines for the map \nand Step Inc. for all the industries and traincars and the forklift annex.",
    "collection": "map",
    "thumbnail": "/img/derivatives/simple/wnyp_revision_2_v1_00/thumbnail.jpg",
    "permalink": "/map/wnyp_revision_2_v1_00",
    "lunr_id": 215
  },
